The bug in `CoreOperationCompare` has been investigated, fixed, and verified.

### Cause of the Bug
When evaluating equality (`=`) or inequality (`!=`) comparisons in [`CoreOperationCompare.equal`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jxpath_6_group_a_blind/src/java/org/apache/commons/jxpath/ri/compiler/CoreOperationCompare.java#L45-L83), the operands `left` and `right` are computed. When referencing a variable containing multiple values (e.g. `$d` pointing to `new String[] { "a", "b" }`), the variable evaluates to an [`InitialContext`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jxpath_6_group_a_blind/src/java/org/apache/commons/jxpath/ri/axes/InitialContext.java) representing the collection.

The previous logic checked:
```java
if (l instanceof InitialContext || l instanceof SelfContext) {
    l = ((EvalContext) l).getSingleNodePointer();
}
```
Extracting `getSingleNodePointer()` on the `InitialContext` returned the unindexed `VariablePointer` containing the entire collection as a single object (and not an `Iterator`). This bypassed the iterator comparison logic (`contains((Iterator) l, r)`), evaluating `$d = 'a'` by comparing the `String.valueOf(new String[]{"a", "b"})` against `"a"`, which failed.

### Fix
Updated [`CoreOperationCompare.java`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jxpath_6_group_a_blind/src/java/org/apache/commons/jxpath/ri/compiler/CoreOperationCompare.java) to reset the [`InitialContext`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jxpath_6_group_a_blind/src/java/org/apache/commons/jxpath/ri/axes/InitialContext.java) position (leaving it as an iterable context conforming to XPath multi-valued comparison semantics) and only extract `getSingleNodePointer()` for [`SelfContext`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jxpath_6_group_a_blind/src/java/org/apache/commons/jxpath/ri/axes/SelfContext.java):
```java
if (l instanceof InitialContext) {
    ((EvalContext) l).reset();
}

if (l instanceof SelfContext) {
    l = ((EvalContext) l).getSingleNodePointer();
}
```
(Applied symmetrically to both `l` and `r` operands).

### Verification
* Ran `export TZ='America/Los_Angeles' && defects4j test -t org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.compiler.VariableTest::testIterateVariable`: **0 failing tests**.
* Ran full test suite with `export TZ='America/Los_Angeles' && defects4j test`: **0 failing tests**.
* Generated the patch file [`blind_fix.patch`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jxpath_6_group_a_blind/blind_fix.patch) containing only the changes to `CoreOperationCompare.java`.
